          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#ClaimsAndRetractions"} Claims and retractions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#mzm_in_nanowires"} MZM in nanowires
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesNonDetection"} Non-Detection
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#AnyonsInTopologicalSuperconductorsReferences"} Anyons in topological superconductors
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+states"} ground states
            of certain effectively 1-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+materials"} quantum materials
            (quantum/nano-wires) which are acted on by a “Majorana operator” (namely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+operator"} Hermitian
            combination
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo +
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mo †
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c + c^\dagger
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/canonical+anti-commutation+relations"} annihilation/creation operators
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+relativity"} relativistic
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinors"} Majorana spinors
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+anyons"} Majorana anyons
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adiabatic+theorem"} adiabatic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
            operations in the usual sense, see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "https://quantumcomputing.stackexchange.com/q/25638/19363"} here
          %p
            These Majorana zero modes were theoretically introduced in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+chain"} spin chain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28in+theoretical+physics%29"} model
            by
            %a{:href => "#Kitaev01"} Kitaev 2001
            (“Kitaev spin chain”), originally as a theoretical toy example for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass+gap"} gapped
            and degenerate
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+states"} ground states
            vaguely as expected for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+order"} topological order
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconductors"} superconductors
            with certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+insulators"} topological insulators
            by
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#FuKane08"} Fu &amp; Kane 2008
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experimental
            realization in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superconductor"} super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semiconductor"} semi-conducting
            nano-wires has been proposed in
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#LutchynSayDasSarma10"} Lutchyn, Say &amp; Das Sarma 2010
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#OregRefaelvonOppen10"} Oreg, Refael, von Oppen 2010
          %p#Following
            Following these proposals — and especially after
            %a{:href => "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/research-area/quantum-computing"} Microsoft Quantum
            (with
            %a{:href => "https://qutech.nl/"} QuTech
            at TU Delft) declared (
            %a{:href => "https://blogs.microsoft.com/ai/microsoft-doubles-quantum-computing-bet/"}> Nov 2016
            ) the concrete aim of realizing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+computation"} topological quantum computation
            based on topological qbits given by such “Majorana zero modes” (following the plan laid out in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#DasSarmaFreedmanNayak15"} Das Sarma, Freedman &amp; Nayak 15
            %a{:href => "https://scholar.google.com/scholar?cites=12195292414684872731&as_sdt=2005&sciodt=0,5&hl=en"} enormous attention
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/solid+state+physics"} solid state physics
          %h2#ClaimsAndRetractions Claims and retractions
          %p#But But prominent claims of experimental detection of (these kinds of) Majorana zero modes had to be retracted:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-021-00612-z"}
                  by
                  %em Nature
                  in 2021
              %p
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-021-03373-x"}> doi:10.1038/s41586-021-03373-x
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4587841"} doi:10.5281/zenodo.4587841
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.4545812"} doi:10.5281/zenodo.4545812
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.delta.tudelft.nl/article/majorana-not-fraud-confirmation-bias#"} TU Delft press release
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://retractionwatch.com/2022/04/24/authors-retract-second-majorana-paper-from-nature/"}
                  by
                  %em Nature
                  in 2022
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-022-04704-2"}> doi:10.1038/s41586-022-04704-2
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "https://retractionwatch.com/2022/11/17/another-majorana-particle-paper-retracted-this-time-from-science/"}
                  by
                  %em Science
                  in 2022
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/science.adf7575"}> doi:10.1126/science.adf7575
                \&amp;rbrack;, cf. further commentary by
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+M.+Frolov"} S.M. Frolov
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a{:href => "https://espressospin.org/2022/11/17/the-fallen-angel-particle/"} here
          %p or had an “Editorial Expression of Concern” attached to them:
          %ul
            %li
              by
              %em Nature communications
              in 2025 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-025-58136-3"}> doi:10.1038/s41467-025-58136-3
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            and a range of further claims are under similar criticism, see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6344447"} Frolov &amp; Mourik 2020
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DasSarmaPan21"} Das Sarma &amp; Pan 2021
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6325378"} Frolov, Mourik &amp; Zuo 2022
            %a{:href => "#Mourik24"} Mourik 2024
            and the extensive list
            %a{:href => "https://twitter.com/spinespresso/status/1503352928656138241"} here
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "https://bsky.app/profile/spinespresso.bsky.social/post/3likchwf3p22d"} here
          %p
            While many researchers began to dismiss the whole approach of “Majorana zero modes” (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#BSSA21"} BSSA21
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2106.11840v4.pdf#page=3"} p. 3
            %a{:href => "#Nayak22"} Nayak 22
            \&amp;
            %a{:href => "#MicrosoftQuantum23"} MicrosoftQuantum 23
            – but see the
            %a{:href => "#MicrosoftQuantum23Caveat"} journal’s editorial caveat
            and cautionary commentary by
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FrolovMourik22a"} Frolov &amp; Mourik 22a
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FrolovMourik22a"} 22b
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Frolov22"} Frolov 22
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#DasSarma22"} Das Sarma 22, p. 9
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Mourik23"} Mourik 23
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Legg24"} Legg 24
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Legg25"} Legg 25
          %p
            On
            %a{:href => "https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/quantum/2025/02/19/microsoft-unveils-majorana-1-the-worlds-first-quantum-processor-powered-by-topological-qubits/"} 19 Feb 2025
            a Microsoft Azure press release announced a quantum chip (“
            %em> Majorana 1
            ”) alleged to host a couple of topologically protected qbits. The accompanying Nature article
            %a{:href => "#AzureFeb25"} Microsoft Azure Quantum 2025
            states more carefully that:
          %blockquote
            %p
              “
              %em> These measurements do not, by themselves, determine whether the low-energy states detected by interferometry are topological.
              ”
          %p
            and again the journal issued a
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#AzureFeb25Caveat"} caveat
          %p
            In fact, the referee reports for
            %a{:href => "#AzureFeb25"} Microsoft Azure Quantum 2025
            were made available (
            %a{:href => "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-024-08445-2/MediaObjects/41586_2024_8445_MOESM2_ESM.pdf"}> pdf
            ) and say:
          %blockquote
            %p &amp;lbrack;editorial team&amp;rbrack;: “the results in this manuscript do not represent evidence for the presence of Majorana zero modes”
            %p &amp;lbrack;referee 1&amp;rbrack;: “rather misleading way in which these data are presented and the extreme simplifications of the modeling which, essentially, assumes a topological state and includes Majoranas by hand, yet again forcing an a priori interpretation of the data. […] There is no definitive proof of topology or qubit…”
            %p &amp;lbrack;referee 2&amp;rbrack;: “the relationship to Majorana physics is not completely certain and needs some serious scrutiny”
            %p &amp;lbrack;referee 3&amp;rbrack;: “I am firmly convinced this work should not be published in Nature or any other high visibility journal”
          %p
            Technical analysis of the claims is provided by
            %a{:href => "#Legg25"} Legg 2025
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FrolovMourik25"} Frolov &amp; Mourik 2025
          %p
            The accompanying company “roadmap” (
            %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.12252"}> arXiv:2502.12252
