          %h3#ReferencesNonDetection Non-Detection
          %p On the general problem of distinguishing the expected effect from noise:
          %ul
            %li#DasSarmaPan21
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sankar+Das+Sarma"}> Sankar Das Sarma
              , Haining Pan,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Disorder-induced zero-bias peaks in Majorana nanowires
              %strong 103
              195158 (2021) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.05628"}> arXiv:2103.05628
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.103.195158"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.103.195158
          %blockquote
            %p we believe that similar confirmation bias applies to many other topological discovery claims in the literature during 2000–2020 where a precise knowledge of what one is looking for has been the key factor in the discovery claim, with the experimental quantization results themselves not being sufficiently compelling. &amp;lbrack;…&amp;rbrack; Our results certainly apply to most of the Majorana experiments during 2012–2021 in the literature.
          %ul
            %li#BSSA21
              Koen Bertels, Tamara Sarac, Aritra Sarkar, Imran Ashraf,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Computing – from NISQ to PISQ
              %strong 41
              (2021) 24-32 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.11840v4"}> arXiv:2106.11840v4
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.ieeecomputersociety.org/10.1109/MM.2021.3099195"} doi:10.1109/MM.2021.3099195
          %blockquote
            %p
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2106.11840v4.pdf#page=3"}> p. 3
              \: The quantum physics community is sufficiently aware that when certain qubit technologies do not produce any reasonable result after several years of effort, they should be gently removed from the list of quantum candidates. After working with the physics colleagues in Delft, we saw that happening with the Majorana qubits that could not be confirmed in any follow-up experiment.
          %ul
            %li#FrolovMourik22a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+M.+Frolov"}> Sergey M. Frolov
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Mourik"} Vincent Mourik
              %em We cannot believe we overlooked these Majorana discoveries
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2203.17060"}> arXiv:2203.17060
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6364928"} doi:10.5281/zenodo.6364928
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/ftp/arxiv/papers/2203/2203.17060.pdf#page=7"} p. 7
          %p Non-retracted claims of experimental realization of something in the direction of Majorana zero modes:
          %ul
            %li#MMBDRSC19
              %p
                Gerbold C. Ménard, Andrej Mesaros, Christophe Brun, François Debontridder, Dimitri Roditchev, Pascal Simon, Tristan Cren,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Isolated pairs of Majorana zero modes in a disordered superconducting lead monolayer
                %strong 10
                2587 (2019)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-019-10397-5"} doi:10.1038/s41467-019-10397-5
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
            %li#Nayak22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chetan+Nayak"}> Chetan Nayak
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Microsoft has demonstrated the underlying physics required to create a new kind of qubit
            %li#MicrosoftQuantum23
              %p
                M. Aghaee et al. (
                %a{:href => "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/research-area/quantum-computing"}> Microsoft Quantum
                ),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em InAs-Al Hybrid Devices Passing the Topological Gap Protocol
                %strong 107
                245423 (2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.107.245423"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.107.245423
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.02472"} arXiv:2207.02472
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/research/video/inas-al-hybrid-devices-passing-the-topological-gap-protocol/"} video presentation
              %p
                %br/
              %p#MicrosoftQuantum23Caveat with an accompanying caveat editorial:
              %p
                Randall D. Kamien, Jessica Thomas, Stephen E. Nagler, Anthony M. Begley, and Sarma Kancharla,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Editorial: Transparency in Physical Review Articles
                %strong 107
                210001 (2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.107.210001"}> doi:10.1103/PhysRevB.107.210001
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %p saying:
              %blockquote
                %p
                  “In this issue of Physical Review B, Aghaee et al. &amp;lbrack;
                  %a{:href => "#MicrosoftQuantum23"}> 1
                  \&amp;rbrack; report on an advancement towards the goal of topological quantum computing. While Physical Review readers are well aware that the many minutiæ of procedures, computations, and synthesis may be omitted in any particular dispatch, in this publication the intellectual property of the authors’ employer has prevented the release of some parameters of the studied devices that may be needed in order to reproduce them. As a reflection of the traditional values of the scholarly community, this is not in accordance with the usual norms of the Physical Review journals.”
            %li#AzureFeb25
              %p
                Microsof Azure Quantum:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interferometric single-shot parity measurement in InAs–Al hybrid devices
                %strong 638
                (2025) 651–655 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41586-024-08445-2"}> doi:10.1038/s41586-024-08445-2
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %p#AzureFeb25Caveat
                again with an accompanying caveat editorial (“Peer Review File” &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://static-content.springer.com/esm/art%3A10.1038%2Fs41586-024-08445-2/MediaObjects/41586_2024_8445_MOESM2_ESM.pdf"}> pdf
                \&amp;rbrack;):
              %blockquote
                %p “The editorial team wishes to point out that the results in this manuscript do not represent evidence for the presence of Majorana zero modes in the reported devices. The work is published for introducing a device architecture that might enable fusion experiments using future Majorana zero modes.”
          %p but see commentary in:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+Frolov"}> Sergey Frolov
                ,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://twitter.com/spinespresso/status/1671558089382957056"} Twitter:1671558089382957056
                (21 June 2023)
            %li
              %p
                Karmela Padavic-Callaghan,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Microsoft says its weird new particle could improve quantum computers — Researchers at Microsoft say they have created elusive quasiparticles called Majorana zero modes – but scientists outside the company are sceptical
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.newscientist.com/article/2378782-microsoft-says-its-weird-new-particle-could-improve-quantum-computers"} web
            %li#Mourik23
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Mourik"}> Vincent Mourik
                \: correspondence with PRX editorial team on what later was published as
                %a{:href => "#MicrosoftQuantum23"} MS23
                (2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://pubpeer.com/publications/4C7F25D6DFE392856EF4171E379D67"}> pubpeer
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Legg25
              %p
                Henry F. Legg:
                %em Comment on “InAs-Al hybrid devices passing the topological gap protocol”, Microsoft Quantum, Phys. Rev. B 107, 245423 (2023)
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.19560"}> arXiv:2502.19560
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#FrolovMourik25
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+M.+Frolov"}> Sergey M. Frolov
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Mourik"} Vincent Mourik
                %em Majorana Fireside Chat: HOW CLOSE ARE WE TO A TOPOLOGICAL QUBIT?
                (Feb 2025) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/9Ag-L3hZiXo"}> YT
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p and earlier:
          %ul
            %li#FrolovMourik22b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+M.+Frolov"}> Sergey M. Frolov
                ,
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vincent+Mourik"} Vincent Mourik
                %em Majorana Fireside Podcast, Episode 1: The Microsoft TGP paper live review
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RnYghkDaHH0"}> video
                , conclusion at:
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RnYghkDaHH0&t=3691s"} 1:01:31
              %blockquote
                %p
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/RnYghkDaHH0?t=3712"} 1:01:52
                  The signal is fully consistent, from what we see, with
                  %em not
                  having discovered any Majorana or topological superconductivity here. At the same time, the amount of data is extremely narrow.
            %li#Frolov22
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+M.+Frolov"}> Sergey M. Frolov
                ,
                %em Superconductors and semiconductors, nanowires and majorana, research and integrity
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=FR7J4yH67GA"}> video
                , general caution:
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/FR7J4yH67GA?t=3334"} 55:34
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/FR7J4yH67GA?t=3701"} 1:01:41
              %blockquote
                %p
                  %a{:href => "https://youtu.be/FR7J4yH67GA?t=3710"}> 1:01:50
                  \: The claims of the discovery of Majorana have been overblown and are false. Majorana has not been discovered in nanowires. I don’t believe in any other system it has been discovered either.
          %p On how this could happen:
          %ul
            %li
              Elizabeth Gibney,
              %em Inside Microsoft’s quest for a topological quantum computer
              (Interview with Alex Bocharov), Nature (2016) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1038/nature.2016.20774"}> doi:10.1038/nature.2016.20774
              \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p &amp;lbrack;Bocharov:&amp;rbrack; We’re people-centric, rather than problem-centric.
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#Frolov21
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergey+M.+Frolov"}> Sergey M. Frolov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em So, You Think You Discovered a New State of Matter?
                %strong 14
                68 (2021) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://physics.aps.org/articles/v14/68"}> physics.aps:v14/68
